course: dictionary
lesson: 15643
title: Textual evidence
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Textual means to do with a text, which is the actual written words of a book, poem or document. When a teacher asks about the textual details, she wants the exact words on the page.
explain: Textual evidence is words or lines taken from a text to prove what you say about it. If someone asks, «How do you know Mia is nervous?», you can point to a line such as «Her hands shook as she opened the letter.»
explain: Always copy the evidence exactly and put it in quotation marks. Then explain how it proves your point, because evidence on its own is only half an answer.
fact: Textual means to do with the actual written words of a text.
fact: «Textual evidence» means words or lines taken from a text to support a point.
fact: In English lessons, you show textual evidence by quoting the exact words in quotation marks.
fact: In history and Bible study, «textual» can describe studying the exact words of old writings.
fact: Common phrases include «textual evidence», «textual analysis» and «textual details».
exercise: What does textual mean? | Your own feelings about the story | Pictures on the cover of a book | *The actual written words of a text | The weather in the story
exercise: Which line is good textual evidence that the dog is scared? | *«It flattened its ears and hid under the table.» | Dogs are often kept as pets. | The sun was shining over the park that day. | The dog was brown and had a red collar.
exercise: In a history lesson, what can «textual» describe? | Maps of the moon | *The exact words of old writings | The shape of old castles | Music played at a festival
test: Which phrase means words copied from a story to prove a point? | Text message | *Textual evidence | Textual weather | Plot twist
test: Why should you put textual evidence in quotation marks? | *So the reader knows the exact words come from the text | Teachers like to see them | It makes the answer look longer | Quotation marks make the words louder
exam: A pupil writes «Ben is brave» with no evidence. What is missing? | *Textual evidence: the exact words from the text that prove Ben is brave | A longer title for the essay | Nothing is missing | A picture of Ben
